window_algorithm", "label": "Sliding Window Algorithm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/content/module-50/02-case-rate-limiter.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_content_module_50_02_case_rate_limiter_fixed_window_algorithm", "label": "Fixed Window Algorithm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/content/module-50/02-case-rate-limiter.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_content_module_50_02_case_rate_limiter_thread_safety_race_condition", "label": "Thread Safety / Race Condition in Rate Limiter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/content/module-50/02-case-rate-limiter.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In-memory Map read-modify-write on bucket tokens is not atomic under concurrency, letting too many requests through; production uses atomic counters or distributed locks (Redis INCR)."}, {"id": "src_content_module_50_02_case_rate_limiter_redis_incr", "label": "Redis INCR (atomic counter)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/content/module-50/02-case-rate-limiter.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_content_module_50_02_case_rate_limiter_yagni_vs_known_variation", "label": "Strategy Justified Despite YAGNI", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/content/module-50/02-case-rate-limiter.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "YAGNI applies only without a real signal for variation; rate limiting is a domain with known multiple algorithms (fixed window, sliding window, token bucket, leaky bucket) with different trade-offs, so a swappable interface up front is justified."}], "edges": [{"source": "src_content_mod